  "prefLabel": "Plc 2101.02 Applicability",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 2101.02 Applicability.\n\n(a) The rules in this chapter shall apply to disputes, regardless of whether the consumer or a different party initiates the dispute:\n\n(1) That arise from the need to correct or repair defects in manufactured houses that are reported during the one-year period beginning on the date of installation; and\n\n(2) For which the parties have elected to use the ADR procedures available under Plc 2100.\n\n(b) No person shall be required to use the ADR procedures available under Plc 2100.\n\nSource. #14331, eff 8-20-25, EXPIRES: 8-20-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc2100.html"
}
